  "proofs": [
    "Actual native SDK/server/worker admission write failure sends no SIP INVITE. Operational readiness reports the worker failure, and the original logical request replays its one accepted leg receipt after fixture repair.",
    "An injected malformed stored Session reaches the actual resolver as a 503. The worker propagates it as infrastructure failure rather than falsely acknowledging a remote origination rejection; no INVITE or start admission exists.",
    "Production activation/cleanup logic composed with an actual Store preserves uncertain state after failed cleanup, prevents dispatch replay and recovery redispatch, and drops the owned activation future.",
    "The stalled cleanup injection returns uncertain within the worker drain budget and drops both cleanup and activation futures. Current backing-credential revocation during activation invokes cleanup and records cancellation.",
    "A task-authorized invocation created through trusted Store fixture setup sends an actual loopback SIP INVITE. Owner cancellation reaches the SIP peer as CANCEL; the leg becomes cancelled; the cancelled invocation replay fails; ordinary native SDK messaging continues in the same conversation.",
    "The extracted shared SIP fixture preserves all three existing Gate 3 SIP media/terminal behavior tests. The final all-suite run passed all available workspace tests within their stated scopes."
  ],
  "review": {
    "structure": "The production worker remains 241 lines; the 49-line activation helper owns bounded cancellation observation/cleanup. Fault injection uses disposable fixture data/futures, with no production test flags. Shared loopback fixture extraction keeps separate integration tests focused.",
